body:
@wiredfool I'm going to guess that recent changes made to Image.py caused opening invalid files to end up in FliImagePlugin somehow… when the `open()` should never make it that far. Here's the  entire `_accept` method that fails:

```
def _accept(prefix):
    return i16(prefix[4:6]) in [0xAF11, 0xAF12]
```

I can't imagine that code has changed much. Though being more careful there would be nice too.
